From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jorge Ramirez-Ortiz <jorge.ramirez@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kodiak-el2: fix DSP firmware-name; enable
 venus (WIP)

This kernel already carries the Kodiak EL2 overlay (commit "arm64: dts:
qcom: kodiak: Add EL2 overlay"), but the adsp/cdsp remoteproc nodes
inherit firmware-name = "qcom/qcs6490/<x>.mbn" from the base RB3Gen2 DTS.
linux-firmware ships the RB3Gen2 DSP images under qcom/qcm6490/, so the
PAS driver's request_firmware() fails with -ENOENT and the remoteproc
never reaches the OP-TEE PAS authenticate/reset step (so it looks like
the kernel "never calls OP-TEE for PAS").

Override the adsp/cdsp firmware-name to qcom/qcm6490/ in the EL2 overlay
so the images are found and PAS-over-OP-TEE proceeds.

WARNING: UNDER DEVELOPMENT.  The &venus enablement (status, SMMU stream
mappings and the video-firmware subnode) is experimental and not yet
validated on Kodiak.  The IOMMU stream IDs and the firmware-loading path
are still being worked out; expect this hunk to change.

Signed-off-by: Jorge Ramirez-Ortiz <jorge.ramirez@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kodiak-el2.dtso b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kodiak-el2.dtso
index 0b3a69a0d765..1632ed7968a0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kodiak-el2.dtso
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kodiak-el2.dtso
@@ -14,10 +14,18 @@
 };
 
 &remoteproc_adsp {
+	/*
+	 * The base RB3Gen2 DTS firmware-name points at qcom/qcs6490, which
+	 * carries no flat adsp.mbn; the RB3Gen2 firmware namespace is qcm6490.
+	 * Without this the PAS driver's request_firmware() fails with -ENOENT
+	 * and the remoteproc never reaches the OP-TEE PAS authenticate step.
+	 */
+	firmware-name = "qcom/qcm6490/adsp.mbn";
 	iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x1800 0x0>;
 };
 
 &remoteproc_cdsp {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/qcm6490/cdsp.mbn";
 	iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x11a0 0x0400>;
 };
 
@@ -27,7 +35,14 @@
 };
 
 &venus {
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
+
+	iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x2180 0x20>,
+		 <&apps_smmu 0x2184 0x20>;
+
+	video-firmware {
+		iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x21a2 0x0>;
+	};
 };
 
 &watchdog {
--
